Tooltip_SolarEnergyArray_05=After activating Wireless Mode, Dynamo Hatches are no longer needed.
NameSubstanceReshapingDevice=Substance Reshaping Device
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_MachineType=Substance Reshaping Device
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_Controller=Controller block for the Substance Reshaping Device
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_00=Void begets all things, and chaos forges gods. All matter can be reshaped, but great power cannot be defied.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_01=The laws of the universe are both a cage and a shackle. All things follow the path of entropy—life will inevitably decay, stars will burn out, and dust will return to dust. But we refuse to accept this fate.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_02=They are nameless entities, echoes from beyond reality, remnants we brought back from the unknown when we tampered with the laws of the universe.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_03=We are the creators of stars, the manipulators of reality, and the ultimate masters of gravity!
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_04=Some particles exhibit arrangements that defy known physical rules, some substances exist in ways that violate the laws of thermodynamics.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_05=and some creations… vanish the moment we attempt to document them, as if they never existed at all.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_06=The machine supports cross-recipe parallel processing!
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_07=Supports up to 10 recipes running simultaneously! The optimal ratio for each recipe is 10*10!
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_08=If any recipe exceeds 10 units in operation, it will cause a decrease in total parallel efficiency!
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_09=But remember this—creators are also destroyers.
Tooltip_SubstanceReshapingDevice_10="When the gods fall silent, mortals may seize the mantle of power. But remember, the mantle was never truly ours to claim."
SubstanceReshapingDeviceRecipes=Singularity Stabilization Ring Casings Live:  %s
NameBlueDogMachine=Blue Dog Fountain
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_MachineType=Blue Dog Fountain
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_Controller=Controller Block of Blue Dog Fountain
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_00=In honor of BlueDog — the legendary creator of unofficial mods!
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_01=A legendary device that turns regular water into ultra-pure water — with nothing else!Rumor has it the idea came from a team outing…
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_02=Putting a Hotdog Ingot into the machine seems to get it... a little too excited?
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_03=Oh, and you’d better not look too closely at where the water comes out… It’s not exactly elegant.
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_04=“He doesn’t look very comfortable, does he?”
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_05=“Not really. He might actually be enjoying it…”
Tooltip_BlueDogMachine_06=Enjoy yourself — you’re definitely going to like him!
NameMonkeyShit=The Holy Royal High Priest of Poop Transportation
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_MachineType=The Holy Royal High Priest of Poop Transportation
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_Controller=Controller Block of The Holy Royal High Priest of Poop Transportation
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_00=The Relentless Poop Mover!
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_01=Seriously?! Where on earth did he get all this crap!?
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_02=At times, he walks near the gods... yet strays far from mankind.
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_03=“Please, post something else, I’m begging you!”
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_04=F*** it, you might as well post crap instead of this nonsense!
Tooltip_MonkeyShit_05=Just pour some smelly liquid into the machine — who knows what kind of surprise you’ll get!
NameOrundumDynamo=Orundum Dynamo
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_MachineType=Orundum Dynamo
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_Controller=Controller Block of Orundum Dynamo
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_00=A wondrous device brought from another continent — it runs on pure Originite Prime power!
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_01=It creates an entirely new source of energy!An all-new internal Originium network system!
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_02=Upgrade the coils and glass to achieve greater efficiency and improved parallel performance.
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_03=Every unit of Originite Prime converts into Orundum once it’s used up.
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_04=Completely free from Originium dust contamination!
Tooltip_OrundumDynamo_05=The very dawn of the Originium industry—good luck out there, Administrator!
NameElectricTypeOneMiningMachine=Electric Type-I Mining Machine
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_MachineType=Power Miner
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_Controller=Controller Block of Electric Type-I Mining Machine
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_00=The Electric Type-I Mining Machine is the first piece of equipment you gain access to for fully automated mining of Orundum ore veins.
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_01=Just set the structure on top of the Orundum ore veins unique to Planet Talos and it will start operating!
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_02=The machine requires at least one Originite Prime Main Vein Block within its detection range to operate.
Tooltip_ElectricTypeOneMiningMachine_03=The detection range is a 7×7×3 cubic area that starts one block behind and two blocks below the machine’s main block.
NamePlanter=Planter
Tooltip_Planter_MachineType=Planter
Tooltip_Planter_Controller=Controller Block of Planter
Tooltip_Planter_00=A silo-shaped device capable of cultivating various common plants. Developed in-house by Endfield, it offers real-time monitoring and adjustment of internal lighting, temperature, and plant hormone conditions — its greatest technical advantage.
Tooltip_Planter_01=Comes with 1 parallel slot by default; upgrading the glass casing allows for additional parallel operations.
Tooltip_Planter_02=Operates at 100% work time by default; upgrade the coil to reduce work time.
Tooltip_Planter_03=Can grow the majority of native crops found on Talos-2!
Tooltip_Planter_04=Use together with the Seed Collecting device!
NameSeedCollectingMachine=Seed Collecting Machine
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_MachineType=Seed Collecting Machine
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_Controller=Controller Block of Seed Collecting Machine
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_00=A device designed to collect ordinary plant seeds. On Talos-2, a bountiful harvest is always a cause for great joy.
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_01=Comes with 1 parallel slot by default; upgrading the glass casing allows for additional parallel operations.
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_02=Operates at 100% work time by default; upgrade the coil to reduce work time.
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_03=Can gather the majority of native crops found on Talos-2!
Tooltip_SeedCollectingMachine_04=Use together with the Planter!
NameRefiningFurnace=Refining Furnace
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_MachineType=Refining Furnace
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_Controller=The controller block of the Refining Furnace
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_00=A specialized device that refines other materials at extremely high temperatures.
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_01=Stripping, reshaping... under intense heat, the form of the material changes again and again until it emerges completely renewed.
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_02=Starts with 1 parallel line by default and a work time of 200 ticks.
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_03=Upgrade the coils and glass structure to unlock even greater performance!
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_04=This is not an ordinary furnace! Do not try to stuff random raw materials into it!
Tooltip_RefiningFurnace_05=I hope you’ve stored up enough Orundum energy!
NamePulverizer=Pulverizer
Tooltip_Pulverizer_MachineType=Pulverizer
Tooltip_Pulverizer_Controller=The controller block of the Pulverizer
Tooltip_Pulverizer_00=A heavy-duty industrial device capable of pulverizing various materials.
Tooltip_Pulverizer_01=Do you hear the sound of it chewing through those hard materials?
Tooltip_Pulverizer_02=Machines on Planet Talos can only pulverize items from Planet Talos—makes perfect sense, doesn’t it?
NameAccessoriesMachine=Accessories Machine
Tooltip_AccessoriesMachine_MachineType=Accessories Machine
Tooltip_AccessoriesMachine_Controller=The controller block of the Accessories Machine
Tooltip_AccessoriesMachine_00=A versatile processing platform capable of machining all kinds of parts.
Tooltip_AccessoriesMachine_01=Turning, milling, planing, grinding—precision machining all in one machine.
NameShapingMachine=Shaping Machine
Tooltip_ShapingMachine_MachineType=Shaping Machine
Tooltip_ShapingMachine_Controller=The controller block of the Shaping Machine
Tooltip_ShapingMachine_00=A specialized device capable of stamping and forming various containers.
Tooltip_ShapingMachine_01=After holding a product workshop in collaboration with the Alliance Industrial Union,
Tooltip_ShapingMachine_02=Terminal Land Industries finally overcame the key technical challenge of “mold replacement”.
NameGrinder=Grinder
Tooltip_Grinder_MachineType=Grinder
Tooltip_Grinder_Controller=The controller block of the Grinder
Tooltip_Grinder_00=A specialized device capable of finely grinding various powdered materials.
Tooltip_Grinder_01=This machine traces its origins back to a traditional agricultural processing device from the Yan Kingdom.
NameEncapsulationMachine=Encapsulation Machine
Tooltip_EncapsulationMachine_MachineType=Encapsulation Machine
Tooltip_EncapsulationMachine_Controller=The controller block of the Encapsulation Machine
Tooltip_EncapsulationMachine_00=A specialized device used for encapsulating certain energy components.
Tooltip_EncapsulationMachine_01=Across Talos II, many different forms and designs of batteries once emerged.
Tooltip_EncapsulationMachine_02=After humanity finally escaped the quagmire of war, the production standards for these products gradually became unified.
NameFillingUnit=Filling Unit
Tooltip_FillingUnit_MachineType=Filling Unit
Tooltip_FillingUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Filling Unit
Tooltip_FillingUnit_00=A specialized device capable of precisely filling raw materials into containers.
Tooltip_FillingUnit_01=Its patented aseptic filling technology greatly reduces the risk of product contamination.
NameForgeOfTheSky=Forge of the Sky
Tooltip_ForgeOfTheSky_MachineType=Forge of the Sky
Tooltip_ForgeOfTheSky_Controller=Controller block of the Forge of the Sky
Tooltip_ForgeOfTheSky_00=A specialized device used for synthesizing products related to Xiranite.
Tooltip_ForgeOfTheSky_01=The Earth gives birth to metals. The Sky holds the Forge.
NamePurificationUnit=Purification Unit
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_MachineType=Purification Unit
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Purification Unit
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_00=A precision device used to purify solutions to higher concentrations.
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_01="You know, my friend, our alchemy has such a glorious history. Look out into space..."
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_02="How could our journey and achievements possibly end here?"
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_03="I need a proper environment—an excellent, stable Originium environment."
Tooltip_PurificationUnit_04="That’s your reason for almost blowing a hole through the O.M.V. DiJiang?"
NameReactorCrucible=Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ReactorCrucible_MachineType=Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ReactorCrucible_Controller=Controller block of the Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ReactorCrucible_00=A specialized device used for solid-liquid chemical reactions.
Tooltip_ReactorCrucible_01=Terminal Industries ultimately decided to order a batch of special steel from the southern region of Talos II, produced by the Syndicate.
Tooltip_ReactorCrucible_02=This was done to counter the corrosive failures occurring within their reaction equipment.
NameExpandedCrucible=Expanded Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ExpandedCrucible_MachineType=Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ExpandedCrucible_Controller=Controller block of the Expanded Reactor Crucible
Tooltip_ExpandedCrucible_00=A high-performance device for conducting solid-liquid chemical reactions, equipped with more ports to handle multiple reactions simultaneously.
Tooltip_ExpandedCrucible_01=Higher capacity, greater safety.
Tooltip_ExpandedCrucible_02=This machine supports up to four recipes running in parallel!
NameFluidPumpMK1=Fluid Pump MK1
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK1_MachineType=Fluid Pump
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK1_Controller=Controller block of the Fluid Pump MK1
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK1_00=A basic device used for extracting liquids.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK1_01=The commerce division procured basic pump components, and the manufacturing base added a power-supply module—thus, a pressurized device capable of integration within industrial systems was born.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK1_02=The area beneath the pipeline structure at the rear of the machine must be a liquid source for it to operate!
NameFluidPumpMK2=Fluid Pump MK2
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_MachineType=Fluid Pump
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_Controller=Controller block of the Fluid Pump MK2
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_00=A powered device used for extracting liquids, capable of handling corrosive fluids.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_01=According to rather unreliable reports, engineers involved in developing the Type‑II acid‑resistant pump once whispered concerns about this product in a corner of the O.M.V.DiJiang’s cafeteria.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_02=Admittedly, Precipitation Acid has been proven to be a sufficiently safe material, yet they still worried that it might react uncontrollably with other Angel‑related substances.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_03=Therefore, an emergency‑lock module was added to this model.
Tooltip_FluidPumpMK2_04=The area beneath the pipeline structure at the rear of the machine must be a liquid source for it to operate!
NameElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine=Electric Type‑II Mining Machine
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_MachineType=Electric Mining Machine
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_Controller=Controller block of the Electric Type‑II Mining Machine
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_00=An advanced version of the Electric Type‑I Mining Machine, featuring sharper drill heads and the ability to extract multiple kinds of ores.
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_01=Place the structural core near the primary ore‑vein blocks unique to Planet Talos II to begin operation!
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_02=At least one corresponding primary ore‑vein block must exist within the detection range, otherwise the device cannot start.
Tooltip_ElectricTypeTwoMiningMachine_03=Detection range: from the main block of the machine, extends 1 block backward and 2 blocks downward, covering a 7×7×3 cuboid area.
NameHighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator=High-Density Energy Fluid Generator
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_MachineType=High-Density Energy Fluid Generator
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_Controller=Controller block of the High-Density Energy Fluid Generator
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_00=The High-Density Energy Fluid Generator is an industrial-grade device.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_01=It is dedicated to producing high-energy fluid that can be used directly.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_02=During operation, it first consumes Orundum energy to keep the pumps and control systems stable
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_03=At the same time, EU power is continuously supplied and injected into a fully sealed reaction chamber.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_04=Inside the chamber, the fluid comes into full contact with the injected energy.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_05=It then passes through sequential stages of pressurization, heating, and continuous stirring.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_06=This gradually raises the fluid’s energy level and converts it into a stable high-energy fluid.
Tooltip_HighDensityEnergyFluidGenerator_07=Each recipe run additionally consumes 100000 EU from the Wireless Energy network!
NameIsotopeInfusionReactor=Isotope Infusion Reactor
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_MachineType=Isotope Infusion Reactor
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_Controller=Controller block of the Isotope Infusion Reactor
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_00=Insert radioactive blocks into the left radiation chamber to initialize the isotope infusion process.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_01=The material is transferred through pipelines into the core cavity and heated to bombardment temperature.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_02=Under high pressure, it undergoes neutron-flux treatment and finally outputs high-density liquid or solid materials from the top outlet!
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_03=Typical isotopes include Plutonium‑238, Uranium‑233, Radium, and Technetium.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_04=At upgrade level 0, the maximum parallel recipe count is 4.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_05=When level n ≥ 1, the parallel limit becomes 4^(n+1).
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_06=Base processing time (no upgrade): 800 ticks.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_07=At levels 1–4, processing time shortens roughly geometrically—ensure a sufficiently strong power grid.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_08=At upgrade level ≥ 5, wireless mode processing time is locked at 20 ticks and will not decrease further.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_09=According to an internal lab memo, below this threshold it is usually the server, not the reactor, that melts first.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_10=Engineers once debated enabling multi‑isotope mixing for higher efficiency.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_11=The plan was abandoned after a joint statement from the “Demolition Team (refusing to sign)” and the “Janitorial Staff (refusing to work overtime)”—the feature remains sealed beneath a coffee stain on the blueprint.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_12=Friendly reminder: do not drink the reactor’s output or barbecue on top of it.
Tooltip_IsotopeInfusionReactor_13=If you hear the material whispering its own name, shut down the power immediately and contact your nearest Radiation Safety Office.
NameGasDiffuser=Gas Diffuser
Tooltip_GasDiffuser_MachineType=Gas Diffuser
Tooltip_GasDiffuser_Controller=Controller block of the Gas Diffuser
Tooltip_GasDiffuser_00=It is a device that can disperse continuously‑input gas around itself, thereby changing the surrounding environmental state.
Tooltip_GasDiffuser_01=It only changes the surroundings during its effective operation and will not cause any harm to the actual environment.
Tooltip_GasDiffuser_02="This thing is not for you to use as an air purifier, and please don’t pour perfume into it next time, okay?"
NameFluid_GasTransmutingUnit=Fluid-Gas Transmuting Unit
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_MachineType=Fluid-Gas Transmuting Unit
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Fluid-Gas Transmuting Unit 
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_00=When activated by a steady input of Liquid Xiranite, this facility can transmute fluid materials into gas, and vice versa.
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_01=A special facility that can transmute materials into another state.
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_02=The process may sound simple, but every single component of the facility, down to the most basic thermometer, is the pinnacle of modern Originium Arts and technology.
Tooltip_Fluid_GasTransmutingUnit_03=The Liquid Xiranite input hatch is located in a dedicated input slot at the center of the machine.
NameSolid_GasTransmutingUnit=Solid-Gas Transmuting Unit
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_MachineType=Solid-Gas Transmuting Unit
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Solid-Gas Transmuting Unit
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_00=When activated by a steady input of Xiragen, this facility can transmute solid materials into gas, and vice versa.
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_01=A special facility that can transmute materials into another state. During the design phase, the engineers accessed every
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_02=entry on Originium Arts and technology in the SOW database. Successful recovery of data lost during the Aggeloi War
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_03=provided crucial inspiration for the scientists today.
Tooltip_Solid_GasTransmutingUnit_04=The Liquid Xiranite input hatch is located in a dedicated input slot at the center of the machine.
NameGasReactorGlobe=Gas Reactor Globe
Tooltip_GasReactorGlobe_MachineType=Gas Reactor Globe
Tooltip_GasReactorGlobe_Controller=Controller block of the Gas Reactor Globe
Tooltip_GasReactorGlobe_00=A facility for performing gas-phase reactions.
Tooltip_GasReactorGlobe_01="The facility must be completely hermetic and include thermostats, humidity controllers, and separator modules.
Tooltip_GasReactorGlobe_02="You think I'm complaining about design challenges? No. In fact, I'm planning to fit a self-destruct module into this contraption."
NameHydroMiningRig=Hydro Mining Rig
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_MachineType=Hydro Mining Rig
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_Controller=Controller block of the Hydro Mining Rig
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_00=A mining rig for digging up various types of ore such as Cuprium Ore. This rig does not need power as it can be driven with Clean Water.
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_01=The Endfield Hydro Mining Rig features a special coating to minimize the riskof rusting in humid/wet environments.
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_02=Place the structural core near the primary ore‑vein blocks unique to Planet Talos II to begin operation!
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_03=At least one corresponding primary ore‑vein block must exist within the detection range, otherwise the device cannot start.
Tooltip_HydroMiningRig_04=Detection range: from the main block of the machine, extends 1 block backward and 2 blocks downward, covering a 7×7×3 cuboid area.
NameGasExtractor=Gas Extractor
Tooltip_GasExtractor_MachineType=Gas Extractor
Tooltip_GasExtractor_Controller=Controller block of the Gas Extractor
Tooltip_GasExtractor_00=It does not require power to work.
Tooltip_GasExtractor_01=A facility that can extract Inergen and other gases.
Tooltip_GasExtractor_02=Those companies would never realize why Endfield Industries bought up all those vacuum cleaner patents.
Tooltip_GasExtractor_03=Place the structural core near the primary ore‑vein blocks unique to Planet Talos II to begin operation!
Tooltip_GasExtractor_04=At least one corresponding primary ore‑vein block must exist within the detection range, otherwise the device cannot start.
Tooltip_GasExtractor_05=Detection range: based on the machine’s main block, extending 2 blocks backward and covering a 7×7×3 cubic area downward.
NameSeparatingUnit=Separating Unit
Tooltip_SeparatingUnit_MachineType=Separating Unit
Tooltip_SeparatingUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Separating Unit
Tooltip_SeparatingUnit_00=A facility that physically disassembles various items.
Tooltip_SeparatingUnit_01=Eighty percent of those who first heard the story of the separating unit simply refused to believe this fact: 
Tooltip_SeparatingUnit_02=The design of this facility was inspired by large UWST disassembling stations for sawing and cutting apart Aggeloi carcasses.
NameGearingUnit=Gearing Unit
Tooltip_GearingUnit_MachineType=Gearing Unit
Tooltip_GearingUnit_Controller=Controller block of the Gearing Unit
Tooltip_GearingUnit_00=A facility that laminates different materials together to create gear components.
Tooltip_GearingUnit_01=A top-tier piece of equipment must undergo multiple processing steps that include textile weaving and compression lamination of various fabric and lining.
NameLargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine=AG-07 Large Force-Contained Proliferation Mine
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_MachineType=AG-07 Large Force-Contained Proliferation Mine
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_Controller=Controller block of the AG-07 Large Force-Contained Proliferation Mine
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_00=Uses precision computer control and force-field containment for fast, batch-scale production of high-purity minerals.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_01=Place the main ore block at the bottom-center of each of the four containers. If not placing the ore block, place the corresponding placeholder block instead. Check NEI or the blueprint for exact positions.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_02=Each container only outputs its corresponding contents. Ensure each container has an output bus before operation! Check NEI or the blueprint for exact positions.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_03=Once activated, each active chamber consumes 150 Internal Universe Computing Power.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_04=To meet quarterly targets, the night shift secretly bumped the central computer's power by fifteen percent to see how much extra they could get.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_05=Output did double, but every single ore grew into hollow tubes – completely useless for standard smelting.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_06=To make it worse, those hollow tubes fit perfectly into coffee mugs – so they got repurposed as custom drinkware, and nobody complained about the yield after all.
Tooltip_LargeForce_ContainedProliferationMine_07=The overclock feature was eventually removed, but replaced with a "morph-optimization algorithm" to control growth shapes.
NameInternalizedUniverseComputingEngine=Internalized Universe Computing Engine
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_MachineType=Orundum Computer
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_Controller=Controller block of the Internalized Universe Computing Engine
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_00=A machine that provides basic Orundum-internalized universe computing power, by retrieving information from the internalized universe within Orundum to generate computation.
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_01=Simple, isn't it? Just supply power and feed it some Orundum, and you'll get 200 points of computing power from the internalized universe.
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_02=In theory, the computing engine extracts "universal fundamental information" from Orundum, but what actually comes out is always baffling.
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_03=One piece of Orundum output nothing but a shopping list: "three pounds of apples, two pounds of pork, and a dozen eggs."
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_04=Another piece was even more absurd — the extraction turned out to be the complete genome sequence of the neighbor's dog.
Tooltip_InternalizedUniverseComputingEngine_05=In the end, everyone concluded that Orundum doesn't store cosmic truths — it stores all the mundane everyday life of this world.
NameXiraniteSolarPowerGenerator=Xiranite Solar Power Generator
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_MachineType=Xiranite Solar Power Generator
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_Controller=Controller block of the Xiranite Solar Power Generator
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_00=By adding Xiranite from Wuling to the machine, engineers finally solved the problem of excessive energy loss in solar power generation.
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_01=Standard output is 1M per 100 ticks. If provided with a Xiranite gas atmosphere, output increases to 1.3x.
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_02=Wuling Clean Energy! Wishing you a clear blue sky!
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_03=The Logistics Department moved a decommissioned Xiranite Solar Power Generator to the employee garden to power it, citing the call for green environmental protection — and also to save on electricity bills.
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_04=As it turned out, the tomatoes in the garden tripled in size to the size of watermelons in just three days. The canteen auntie made a pot of tomato egg drop soup, and somehow managed to serve up the equivalent of ten pots.
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_05=An Agricultural Master came to inspect and suggested that residual Xiranite might have affected plant growth. But the Logistics Department didn't care — they immediately switched to growing cash crops instead.
Tooltip_XiraniteSolarPowerGenerator_06=Now that garden is sealed off, with a sign at the entrance reading "Research Experimental Zone." Inside, they're growing the most expensive spices on the market.
NameProtocolCore=Protocol Core
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_MachineType=Protocol Core
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_Controller=Controller block of the Protocol Core
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_00=The supreme achievement of Endfield Industries, which creates a vast integrated industrial space through the massive Protocol Originium within its structure, and can supply power to integrated industrial machines within its range.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_01=The effective range of the Protocol Core is centered on the current chunk of the main block, extending to a square range of 51×51 chunks.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_02=After joining a player's Originium energy network, you automatically gain the right to use machines within their Protocol Core.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_03=Using machines in a Protocol Core without permission will fail inspection and the machine will be unable to operate.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_04=Warning! Do not frequently turn the Protocol Core on and off! Doing so may cause server lag!
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_05=The Protocol Core logic has been specially optimized — after the first startup, no further scanning operations will be performed.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_06=If this machine only acts as a relay node and does not supply any field to machines, its chunk does not need to be loaded and the link will stay active.
Tooltip_ProtocolCore_07=If this machine needs to provide a field to machines, its chunk must remain loaded (e.g. via a chunkloader); otherwise the field will disappear.
NameRelayTower=Relay Tower
Tooltip_RelayTower_MachineType=Relay Tower
Tooltip_RelayTower_Controller=Controller block of the Relay Tower
Tooltip_RelayTower_00=A relay device capable of wired connections within 500 blocks (absolute distance) to complete power distribution.
Tooltip_RelayTower_01=Can wirelessly supply power to Endfield devices within a small range.
Tooltip_RelayTower_02=The Relay Tower is one of the most expensive devices in the integrated industrial system, with an overall design philosophy closer to that of the Protocol Core.
Tooltip_RelayTower_03=Use an Energy Connector and right-click the controller block to start linking, then left-click another Relay Tower / Power Post to complete the link.
Tooltip_RelayTower_04=Linking from a Protocol Core / Secondary Core also requires the use of an Energy Connector.
Tooltip_RelayTower_05=If this machine only acts as a relay node and does not supply any field to machines, its chunk does not need to be loaded and the link will stay active.
Tooltip_RelayTower_06=If this machine needs to provide a field to machines, its chunk must remain loaded (e.g. via a chunkloader); otherwise the field will disappear.
NameElectricPylon=Electric Pylon
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_MachineType=Electric Pylon
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_Controller=Controller block of the Electric Pylon
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_00=When powered, it can wirelessly supply power to Endfield devices within a relatively large range.
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_01=Capable of short-distance power transmission within 100 blocks (absolute distance).
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_02="Wireless power supply" is Endfield Industries' greatest technological breakthrough. This technology is an extension of Protocol technology and serves as the operational foundation of the entire integrated industrial system.
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_03=Use an Energy Connector and right-click the controller block to start linking, then left-click another Relay Tower / Electric Pylon to complete the link.
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_04=Linking from a Protocol Core / Secondary Core also requires the use of an Energy Connector.
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_05=If this machine only acts as a relay node and does not supply any field to machines, its chunk does not need to be loaded and the link will stay active.
Tooltip_ElectricPylon_06=If this machine needs to provide a field to machines, its chunk must remain loaded (e.g. via a chunkloader); otherwise the field will disappear.
NameXirangAssembler=Xirang Assembler
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_MachineType=Xirang Assembler
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_Controller=Controller block of the Xirang Assembler
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_00=A high-precision assembly machine that performs fine assembling inside an active Xirang gas environment--the "final pair of hands" of the production line.
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_01=Only operates in an active Xirang gas atmosphere; the living soil gas acts as the precision assembly medium, and allegedly doubles as "seasoning" for the parts.
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_02=R&D first tried ordinary air and the yield rate stayed stuck at 40%%. A Wuling master craftsman happened to pass by, took one sniff of the workshop, and said: "The parts need to steep in Xirang gas first."
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_03=After switching to Xirang gas, the yield rate shot up to 99.8%%. Now the entire workshop smells faintly of fresh soil, and the workers swear the finished parts really do come out... smoother.
Tooltip_XirangAssembler_04=The canteen auntie later moved her rice cooker into the workshop, insisting that rice steamed in this atmosphere tastes extra fragrant. Wuling production line--every inch of soil counts.

#DysonSphere
NameDysonCore=Dyson Core
Tooltip_DysonCore_MachineType=Dyson Core
Tooltip_DysonCore_Controller=Controller block of the Dyson Core
Tooltip_DysonCore_00=The craziest project of Endfield Industry - put a star in a box. One core per player; a second one gets you politely shut down.
Tooltip_DysonCore_01=The core burns no fuel, holds no battery, and draws no power. It just stands under the Talos sky.
Tooltip_DysonCore_02=Its job is to be the master switch for its modules. Its hardest work, allegedly, is counting stars.
Tooltip_DysonCore_03=Module slots unlock with your team's paste progress: 0 / 500k / 1M / 1.5M / completed to 8 / 12 / 16 / 20 / 32 slots. The final 12 slots open only on the day the shell is finished.
Tooltip_DysonCore_04=Every module must stay inside the Orundum power field; leaving Talos 2 shuts the core down instantly.
Tooltip_DysonCore_05=Heartbeat signals keep modules alive: after a shutdown or chunk unload, modules disconnect within 2 seconds.
Tooltip_DysonCore_06=Consumes 1,000,000 computation from the owner's personal network; insufficient compute shuts the whole core down.
Tooltip_DysonCore_07=The core passively produces Strange Matter from your team's cloud and paste counts, stored as the owner's personal asset.
Tooltip_DysonCore_08=Teammates may each build their own core, all pushing the same team counters.
Tooltip_DysonCore_09=Components are personal property; once launched they belong to the team - leave the team and the sky stays behind.
Tooltip_DysonCore_10=When R&D first hauled the core to Talos, nobody accounted for the star's actual size.
Tooltip_DysonCore_11=Halfway through assembly, the shell turned out smaller than the star. The engineer fixed three revisions overnight.
Tooltip_DysonCore_12=The next morning he announced with dark circles: We have decided to shrink the star.
Tooltip_DysonCore_13=The cafeteria's steamed buns kept shrinking. At 3 AM, half-eaten buns sat on the blueprint desk.
Tooltip_DysonCore_14=Overtime makes you hungry, and hunger makes you misread the scale. - R&D cafeteria files.
Tooltip_DysonCore_15=An intern asked why not rent an existing ring. The manager replied: Rings are rented, but the shell is ours.
Tooltip_DysonCore_16=On completion, the core announces the owner's team and resets every other team's progress.
Tooltip_DysonCore_17=All launching is permanently locked - including for the owner. The orbit is full, and the slingshot goes home.
Tooltip_DysonCore_18=Warning! Don't casually dismantle a completed core: modules lose their heartbeat, counters won't roll back.
Tooltip_DysonCore_19=The final 12 slots unlock after completion, reserved for receiver and future functional modules.
Tooltip_DysonCore_20=The winning core still outputs power at 10^200 - provided it ever recovers from this project.
Tooltip_DysonCore_21=The box that swallowed the sun - presented by Endfield Industry, Seventh Construction Department.
Tooltip_DysonCore_22=Good luck, Administrator.
NameDysonManufacturingModule=Dyson Manufacturing Module
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_MachineType=Dyson Manufacturing Module
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_Controller=Controller block of the Dyson Manufacturing Module
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_00=The production line module that turns raw materials into Dyson Cloud and Frame components - the first pair of hands.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_01=The module footprint expands one layer with input buses and hatches; products go straight into the owner's personal stock.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_02=Fed Originite Prime and Xirang become component stock, with no physical items ejected.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_03=Base round time 30s, base parallel 64; upgrades push the round down to 15 / 10 / 5s.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_04=Parallel goes up to 128 / 512; Parallel III also gives a 20% chance for 100~200x extra output per round.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_05=Costs go to the team Orundum ledger: 1B/t for cloud, 5B/t for frame.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_06=Consumes 10,000 computation; no paste threshold, and it keeps working after completion.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_07=During the first test run, R&D dumped a whole crate of Originite Prime into the hopper.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_08=The machine hummed for thirty seconds and produced a row of Cloud components - everyone thought it was broken because it made no sound.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_09=A veteran craftsman sighed: If our village forge were this quiet, I'd have been out of a job long ago.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_10=Rumor has it a worker once threw snacks into the hopper to test parallel 512; the machine spat out unknown components.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_11=The Safety Department has placed that worker on a watch list.
Tooltip_DysonManufacturingModule_12=Unused components make great heirlooms.
NameDysonLaunchModule=Dyson Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_MachineType=Dyson Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_Controller=Controller block of the Dyson Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_00=Launches the owner's personal components into orbit: 1 component = 1 count, clouds and frames each into their own pool.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_01=Base round time 10s with up to 16 components; upgrades push it to 5 / 2s.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_02=Batch goes up to 64 / 128; with Dual Launch, clouds and frames fire independently, up to 256 per round.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_03=Before Dual Launch, only the priority type is fired (cloud-first / frame-first); no stock means idle, not switching.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_04=Launch costs 10,000 Orundum per component on the team ledger; funds are checked before components are consumed.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_05=Consumes 100,000 computation; needs no hatches, because its true body is a very large slingshot.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_06=After completion all launching is permanently locked - including for the owner. The slingshot goes home.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_07=Engineers first proposed a coilgun; the test projectile fell back onto the pad and smashed three floor tiles.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_08=Change it. To a slingshot. - design meeting minutes, verbatim.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_09=The current module uses a giant mechanical arm that gently tosses components into orbit, accurate to millimeters.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_10=Operators call it the gentle parabola.
Tooltip_DysonLaunchModule_11=Players ask why launching costs Orundum. Finance replies: Throwing accurately is not free.
NameDysonMassLaunchModule=Dyson Mass Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_MachineType=Dyson Mass Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_Controller=Controller block of the Dyson Mass Launch Module
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_00=One 60s round launches ALL of the owner's personal cloud and frame components into orbit.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_01=Mass means exactly that.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_02=Requires the Mass Launch major node; without it the module is just a sculpture.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_03=Clamped by the team's 50k cloud / 500k frame caps; overflow stays in the personal stock.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_04=Costs 10,000 Orundum per component on the team ledger; consumes 100,000 computation.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_05=Permanently disabled after completion. Its finest moment is dumping the last crate into orbit.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_06=R&D originally called it the Dump-Everything Machine; the name became Mass Launch after an executive complained.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_07=The warehouse keeper still calls it the clearance sale.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_08=Its control logic is simple: All of it, right now. No turning back.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_09=A safety officer suggested a confirmation button; the engineer refused on the spot.
Tooltip_DysonMassLaunchModule_10=Someone who clicks Mass Launch needs no second confirmation.
NameDysonReceiverModule=Dyson Receiver Module
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_MachineType=Dyson Receiver Module
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_Controller=Controller block of the Dyson Receiver Module
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_00=Brings the team's power back home.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_01=Before completion, power = cloud x 2^41 + paste x 2^79 (EU/t).
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_02=Settles once per second, crediting P x 20 each time; the pure-cloud route works too.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_03=After completion only the winning team keeps receiving, at a fixed 10^200.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_04=One receiver per team, first come first served; another can take over if the active one fails.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_05=The GUI sets the Orundum share (0-100), splitting output between the Orundum and wireless EU ledgers.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_06=Consumes no computation and needs zero paste. In essence it is a giant satellite dish.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_07=During testing, the numbers exploded instantly and every light in the building flickered for one second.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_08=This dish is a bit strong. - first line of the test report.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_09=The power could blow up the wireless ledger, so the receiver got a splitter valve.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_10=Divide by percentage first, then credit slowly.
Tooltip_DysonReceiverModule_11=The cafeteria lady threw away her solar water heater and asked: When is the home version coming?
